                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3085172e-0f74-4029-834b-5d6113871253",
                        "source_entry_id": "326c2d37-f34b-3437-8e73-6660152772a8",
                        "source_sense_id": "c995c099-f92a-3dbb-93a1-6686bbea646c",
                        "source_sense_description": "een plant van het geslacht Anemone",
                        "target_lang_word": "anemone",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "anemone",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "925a37c3-5627-3030-b95c-ec16f712fbb9",
                                        "entry_id": "fe9b283e-72ec-3e50-afed-99008feddc6e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any plant of the genus Anemone, of the Ranunculaceae (or buttercup) family, such as the windflower."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d6cad2d-79da-4597-808b-6dace08cfcce",
                                                "sense_id": "925a37c3-5627-3030-b95c-ec16f712fbb9",
                                                "text": "Here (it was said) every year the youth Adonis was again wounded to death, and the river ran red with his blood, while the scarlet anemone bloomed among the cedars and walnuts."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1e21dee-6346-4315-b9dc-83296101f437",
                                                "sense_id": "925a37c3-5627-3030-b95c-ec16f712fbb9",
                                                "text": "Then walking slowly forward he read the letter again, murmuring here and there a word. Angry tulips with you darling manflower punish your cactus if you don’t please poor forgetmenot how I long violets to dear roses when we soon anemone meet all naughty nightstalk wife Martha’s perfume. Having read it all […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0179c4cf-62de-4c72-98eb-6ec3d6ec9d90",
                                                "sense_id": "925a37c3-5627-3030-b95c-ec16f712fbb9",
                                                "text": "Among herbs that have traditionally been considered to possess aphrodisiac virtue are, maidenhair, navelwort, anemone, wild poppy, valerian, cyclamen, male fern, pansy, periwinkle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e090e746-3b29-4026-b8f6-2e44e66a8c21",
                                                "sense_id": "925a37c3-5627-3030-b95c-ec16f712fbb9",
                                                "text": "The engagement photos were set in a leafy bower festooned with pink and white roses, anemones, lilies and delphinium, like something straight out of an enchanted garden."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "540a7fd2-a336-3007-8a40-8b1da2668c20",
                                        "entry_id": "fe9b283e-72ec-3e50-afed-99008feddc6e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sea anemone."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "eae98cc0-ebc1-4759-b793-21be893435f1",
                        "source_entry_id": "326c2d37-f34b-3437-8e73-6660152772a8",
                        "source_sense_id": "c995c099-f92a-3dbb-93a1-6686bbea646c",
                        "source_sense_description": "een plant van het geslacht Anemone",
                        "target_lang_word": "anémone",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "anémone",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "05cb2721-e185-3108-a366-09db0caa2e65",
                                        "entry_id": "3c644223-7446-3f4f-9271-d9b3a0e520df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Renonculacée dont la fleur inodore est remarquable par l’éclat et la variété de ses couleurs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "034f7113-fa6a-45f1-9f3a-2fd68c6f3ba7",
                                                "sense_id": "05cb2721-e185-3108-a366-09db0caa2e65",
                                                "text": "L’Inde autrefois nous donna l’anémone,\nDe nos jardins ornement printanier."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3cae46c4-9c2c-4e64-8062-2e7d8158aa4d",
                                                "sense_id": "05cb2721-e185-3108-a366-09db0caa2e65",
                                                "text": "La production de l’anémone, pour les fleurs coupées ou pour le jardin, est importante en Europe de l’Ouest (Pays-Bas, France, Grande-Bretagne), en Italie, en Israël et aux États-Unis."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84caf5a9-fdce-448a-a922-71d079546b77",
                                                "sense_id": "05cb2721-e185-3108-a366-09db0caa2e65",
                                                "text": "Sur les conseils de Bébé, j’achetai un genre d’anémones, des Monna-Lisa, je crois."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2ed19b57-7db4-352b-8192-c22e13467c38",
                                        "entry_id": "3c644223-7446-3f4f-9271-d9b3a0e520df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anémone de mer ; actinie."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ellipsis"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b1c7e48-d7b5-41cb-b0f4-618042a135e7",
                                                "sense_id": "2ed19b57-7db4-352b-8192-c22e13467c38",
                                                "text": "Les canyons hébergent ainsi de nombreux coraux (soixante espèces dans le seul golfe de Gascogne), des anémones, des oursins ou des concombres de mer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
